=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useSettings/useSaveSettings/useVehicles/useCarPreferences +
    useToast/useNavigationGuard/useFormDraft/useTranslation): bound through the P1/S8
    seam GeneralSettingsSource→GeneralSettingsModel. The prod source fires GET /settings,
    GET /vehicles, GET /user-preferences/latest?vehicle_id=, PUT /settings (web request());
    no HTTP in the view. useToast→toast publisher+seam, useNavigationGuard→
    GeneralSettingsNavigationGuard, useFormDraft→GeneralSettingsDraftStore.
  - Composition (web GlassPanel + IconBox + Select/Input/CurrencyInput + DraftRecoveryBanner
    + FadeIn + Save Button):
      • FadeIn/GlassPanel/IconBox -> TSFadeIn / TSGlassPanel / TSIconBox(.accent, gear).
      • header  -> "Application" title + "Units, language, and cost preferences" subtitle
                   + a freshness chip (ADR-013 native add).
      • sync banner -> "Car uses {distance}/{temperature}/{pressure}" (parseSettingEnum)
                   + "Sync from Car" primary button; shown when the car reported a unit.
      • car clock -> read-only "Car clock format: 24-hour/12-hour" note.
      • field grid (web sm:grid-cols-2) -> responsive 1/2-col LazyVGrid:
          Distance/Temperature/Pressure/Preferred-Range/Language/Currency/Locale/
          Time-Zone-Display selects, a Decimal-Precision stepper with live "Preview:
          14.25", a Time-Zone-Override text field + IANA hint, Electricity-Cost +
          Gas-Price currency fields (ISO from the currency glyph) + gas-unit select,
          and a Comparison-MPG number field — every web <Select>/<Input>/<CurrencyInput>.
      • DraftRecoveryBanner -> SettingsDraftBanner (restore note + Discard).
      • Save Button -> SettingsSaveBar (loading while saving) + "Settings saved" chip.
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview):
      loading (skeleton grid) · empty (friendly "No settings found" + retry) ·
      error (message + Retry; cached form kept behind transient errors) ·
      content (the full editor) · stale (freshness chip + "preferences may be out of
      date" band) · offline (cached settings kept + "last saved settings" band + offline chip).
  - i18n (P1/S10): every web t() key reproduced (app.* / toast.* / forms.* / draft.* +
      the bare distance/temperature/pressure/miles/kilometers/celsius/fahrenheit used in
      the sync summary) plus native chrome (freshness.* / state.* / error.* / action.*).
